Two things this licence cannot settle.

First, authorship. Every line of this code was written by an AI, from the
original C sources, with no human writing or reviewing any of it. Under current
US law an AI is not an author and its output is not copyrightable. It is
therefore unclear whether anyone holds copyright in this code, and so unclear
what there is to license. The MIT grant above is offered because a licence has
to say something; to the extent copyright cannot be asserted, treat this as
public domain.

Second, derivation. It is unsettled whether an AI transpilation of copyrighted
source is a derivative work of that source. There is no precedent either way.

What is not unclear: the upstream synthesizers have owners. MacinTalk is Apple's.
DECtalk is FONIX's, which declares it proprietary and confidential. SAM's C
derives from a SoftVoice program. This licence does not reach any of them, and
cannot. Read NOTICE before copying or redistributing anything here.
